From 9db043b85b874e5ce1ea334373a1436ff6efa9f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vigo <77800979+VIGO-VI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:03:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: add GameSir G7 Pro gamepad and IMU driver

Add a USB input driver for the wired GameSir G7 Pro (3537:109b). Interface 0 is vendor-specific; the driver sends the vendor heartbeat and parses report 0x10 for the physical gamepad, raw IMU, and battery.

The IMU is exposed as a separate input device named "... Motion Sensors", following hid-playstation: INPUT_PROP_ACCELEROMETER, ABS_X/Y/Z for the accelerometer, ABS_RX/RY/RZ for the gyroscope, MSC_TIMESTAMP, and per-axis resolution.  The gamepad and sensor devices share the USB serial as uniq, which lets SDL3 pair them and expose SDL_SENSOR_GYRO/ACCEL.

Battery is a power_supply device.  FF_RUMBLE sends the GIP four-motor packet through a workqueue because the FF callback runs in atomic context.
